{"page_id": "olmo_table_tests-78ad48c65a49aaa9ace77fd4121961550742_pg1-p1", "markdown": "# Technical Data Sheet\n\nLupolen 3621 M RM\n\nLinear Low Density Polyethylene\n\nIyondellbasell\n\n一111\n\nProduct Description\n\nLupolen 3621M RM is a new generation hexene linear low density polyethylene for rotational molding. Typical customer applications include agricultural and chemical storage containers and technical parts. This product exhibits excellent ESCR and high impact strength at low temperatures. Lupolen 3621M RM is a UV-stabilized and pelletized polymer. Tests have shown that this material is resisting against the harmful effect of biodiesel fuel*. It is not intended for use in medical and pharmaceutical applications.\n\n* Resistance is based on our latest patented technology\n\nRegulatory Status\n\nFor regulatory compliance information, see Lupolen 3621 M RM Product Stewardship Bulletin (PSB) and Safety_ Data Sheet (SDS).\n\nThis grade is supported for use in drinking water applications.\n\nStatus\n\nAvailability\n\nApplication\n\nMarket\n\nProcessing Method\n\nAttribute\n\nTypical Properties\n\nPhysical\n\nMelt Flow Rate, (190 °C/2.16 kg)\n\nDensity\n\nMechanical\n\nTensile Modulus\n\nTensile Stress at Yield\n\n- 450 10 %\n- 1000 hr\n\nTensile Strain at Break\n\nTensile Strain at Yield\n\nEnvironmental Stress Crack Resistance, Fs\n\nNote: Cond. B, 10% Arkopal N100\n\nFNCT, (6.0 MPa, 2% Arkopal N100, 50 °C)\n\nImpact\n\nTensile Impact Strength\n\nNote: notched, type 1, method A, -30 °C\n\nThermal\n\nVicat Softening Temperature, (A/50 N)\n\nProcessing Parameters\n\nLyondellBasell\n\n# Technical Data Sheet\n\nDate: 3/27/2020\n\nCommercial: Active\n\nAfrica-Middle East; Asia-Pacific; Europe\n\nCrates; Heavy Duty Packaging; Industrial; Industrial Packaging; Intermediate Bulk Containers; Tanks, Industrial\n\nConsumer Products; Industrial Packaging; Industrial, Building & Construction\n\nRotomolding\n\nGood Processability; High ESCR (Environmental Stress Cracking R